{"crc":"d0b96fd8","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is that when `evaluate(False)` is set globally, `Point.__new__` still checks for imaginary coordinates using `im(a)` which requires evaluation. The check `any(a.is_number and im(a) for a in coords)` fails because `im(a)` returns unevaluated `im(Integer(1))` instead of `0`, and `im(Integer(1))` is truthy.\n\nThe fix should be in `sympy/geometry/point.py` to handle the case where `evaluate=False` by checking if the imaginary part is zero in a way that works without evaluation.\n\n# path: sympy/geometry/point.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n        if any(a.is_number and im(a) for a in coords):\n            raise ValueError('Imaginary coordinates are not permitted.')\n=======\n        if any(a.is_number and im(a) is not S.Zero and bool(im(a) != 0) for a in coords):\n            raise ValueError('Imaginary coordinates are not permitted.')\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQWZ6A7NVB67D22X601YN1W","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQWZ6A19ZC6X9T87KCT5CM3"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786434796.722707}
{"crc":"26fcee33","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:d8464ea8e4b4fc4f30588c20a28ee8f596e7d205d49e3c99759d8ace3401bbf8","instance":"01KZQWZF5JZG21HRJBDNEXN3N1","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is that when `evaluate(False)` is set globally, `Point.__new__` still checks for imaginary coordinates using `im(a)` which requires evaluation. The check `any(a.is_number and im(a) for a in coords)` fails because `im(a)` returns unevaluated `im(Integer(1))` instead of `0`, and `im(Integer(1))` is truthy.\n\nThe fix should be in `sympy/geometry/point.py` to handle the case where `evaluate=False` by checking if the imaginary part is zero in a way that works without evaluation.\n\n# path: sympy/geometry/point.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n        if any(a.is_number and im(a) for a in coords):\n            raise ValueError('Imaginary coordinates are not permitted.')\n=======\n        if any(a.is_number and im(a) is not S.Zero and bool(im(a) != 0) for a in coords):\n            raise ValueError('Imaginary coordinates are not permitted.')\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786434796.722782}
